;- says there\u2019s a lot of stress.] [Key Largo Bay Marriott manager John HAVAIRES&#134;- notes the financial impact.] \n (Studio: Tom Brokaw) Hurricane tracking information on msnbc.com noted.", "segment_duration": 280, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63050.0", "legacy_segment_id": 764945, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "5f99PolQy6", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-09", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 764944, "segment_id": "9TlSAMzkpq", "segment_broadcast_id": "5f99PolQy6", "segment_title": "Terrorism / Zawahiri Videotape", "segment_description": "(Studio: Tom Brokaw) Report introduced. \n (Pentagon: Jim Miklaszewski) Al Jazeera\u2019s release of a videotape from Ayman al-Zawahiri, Al Qaeda leader Osama bin Laden\u2019s deputy, featured; tape excerpts shown as Zawahiri\u2019s words of warning for the US are translated; details given of concern about a terror attack in the US. [Military expert William ARKIN&#134;- explains Al Qaeda\u2019s message that they are still out there.]", "segment_duration": 120, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63330.0", "legacy_segment_id": 764946, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "5f99PolQy6", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-09", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 764944, "segment_id": "W8cVKimDxf", "segment_broadcast_id": "5f99PolQy6", "segment_title": "Indonesia / Jakarta Terrorism", "segment_description": "(Studio: Tom Brokaw) A car bombing at the Australian embassy in Jakarta, Indonesia, reported; scenes shown.", "segment_duration": 20, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63450.0", "legacy_segment_id": 764947, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "5f99PolQy6", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-09", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 764944, "segment_id": "nE1ulhAxw7", "segment_broadcast_id": "5f99PolQy6", "segment_title": "Sudan / Genocide", "segment_description": "(Studio: Tom Brokaw) Secretary of State Colin Powell\u2019s declaration that black Africans in the Darfur region of Sudan are victims of genocide supported by the government noted; scenes shown of Sudanese refugees.", "segment_duration": 30, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63470.0", "legacy_segment_id": 764948, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "5f99PolQy6", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-09", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 764944, "segment_id": "V3mz9mIxZD", "segment_broadcast_id": "5f99PolQy6", "segment_title": "Iraq Watch", "segment_description": "(Studio: Tom Brokaw) The US crackdown on cities under insurgent control noted; scenes shown from Fallujah.", "segment_duration": 30, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63500.0", "legacy_segment_id": 764949, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "5f99PolQy6", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-09", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 764944, "segment_id": "JtJjrIzP5B", "segment_broadcast_id": "5f99PolQy6", "segment_title": "Decision 2004 / Bush vs. Kerry / Military Service Records", "segment_description": "(Studio: Tom Brokaw) Report introduced.   (Washington: Andrea Mitchell) The continuing debate over the military service of President Bush & Senator John Kerry featured; details given of questions about the authenticity of documents casting doubt on Bush\u2019s National Guard service and about attacks on Kerry\u2019s anti-war activities. [July, 1999, BUSH \u2013 denies getting special treatment.] [Senator Tom HARKIN&#134;- says the president has got to confront this.] [Former Vietnam prisoner of war Jack FELLOWES&#134;- calls for Kerry to be accountable.] A shift in Bush\u2019s favor in polls in Ohio and Missouri discussed; CNN/\u201cUSA Today\u201d/Gallup poll results cited; map of battleground states shown.", "segment_duration": 190, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63530.0", "legacy_segment_id": 764950, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "5f99PolQy6", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-09", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3,